  "id": "feeling-of-knowing",
  "term": "feeling of knowing",
  "definition": "Feeling of knowing is a state of awareness in recognition memory in which something seems familiar, but the person does not consciously recollect the contextual details or associations linked to it. In this source, it is treated as distinct from recollection and as not sufficient on its own for accurate retrieval of complex episodic memories.",
